  "as_of_notes": "Counts reflect ACTIVE registered voters from the Washington Voter Registration Database (VRDB) monthly snapshot as of June 1, 2026. Source spreadsheet '2026-05 Voter Demographics Tables.xlsx' was published/last-modified 2026-06-01; the statewide Active total of 5,117,470 matches the figure published on the WA SOS site as of June 1, 2026. (Inactive registrations are tracked separately: 419,393 statewide; Active+Inactive = 5,536,863.)",
  "data_quality": "high",
  "notes": "Washington does NOT register voters by party; all by_party fields are null. 'total_registered' uses the ACTIVE registrant count, which is Washington's standard 'registered voters' measure. All 39 counties present; county Active counts sum exactly to the statewide Active total (5,117,470), independently cross-validated against the County-and-Gender and County-and-Age-Group tables in the same workbook. FIPS codes are standard 5-digit state(53)+county codes. Latest available monthly file at time of retrieval; no June-dated file (2026-06) was published yet. Source: 'Voter Demographics Tables (XLSX)' at https://www.sos.wa.gov/sites/default/files/2026-05/2026-05%20Voter%20Demographics%20Tables.xlsx"
